WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:02.422
- [Voiceover] California is experiencing

00:00:02.422 --> 00:00:04.840
its most serious drought in decades.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.131
In about a year, the state's
reservoirs could run dry.

00:00:08.131 --> 00:00:10.183
This is a serious crisis.

00:00:10.183 --> 00:00:13.820
Here's what Californians
are doing to make a change.

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.587
- I really care about the environment,

00:00:15.587 --> 00:00:17.924
that's why I only eat locally grown food,

00:00:17.924 --> 00:00:19.318
like this almond.

00:00:20.256 --> 00:00:22.253
- [Voiceover] But it takes
about 1.1 gallons of water

00:00:22.253 --> 00:00:23.635
to make one almond,

00:00:23.635 --> 00:00:26.073
and that doesn't help because
it was grown in California.

00:00:26.073 --> 00:00:28.231
- Yeah, but isn't the most important thing

00:00:28.231 --> 00:00:29.385
just to eat local?

00:00:29.385 --> 00:00:31.294
- [Voiceover] No, not in this instance.

00:00:31.294 --> 00:00:33.184
- Does it help that I'm vegan?

00:00:33.184 --> 00:00:34.180
- [Voiceover] Let's move on.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:36.191
Let's see what this couple's
doing to make a change.

00:00:36.191 --> 00:00:37.918
- I'm taking my girlfriend on a picnic,

00:00:37.918 --> 00:00:39.706
but instead of taking three jugs of water,

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:40.965
I'm only gonna take two.

00:00:40.965 --> 00:00:41.798
- [Voiceover] Why would you need

00:00:41.798 --> 00:00:43.932
that many jugs of water
in the first place?

00:00:43.932 --> 00:00:45.110
- In case we get thirsty,

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:47.122
or we decide to have a water fight again.

00:00:47.122 --> 00:00:49.214
Babe loves water fights.

00:00:49.214 --> 00:00:51.328
- [Voiceover] This is literally
the worst possible time to--

00:00:51.328 --> 00:00:52.302
- Water fights are great.

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:53.521
They're fun.

00:00:53.521 --> 00:00:54.131
Aren't they fun?

00:00:54.131 --> 00:00:55.065
- Yeah, so fun.

00:00:55.065 --> 00:00:56.386
- Do your water fight thing.

00:00:56.386 --> 00:00:58.448
Show the water fight thing.

00:00:59.657 --> 00:01:00.812
But there's like a water balloon.

00:01:00.812 --> 00:01:01.728
It's so cute.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:02.560
- (laughs) It's so fun.

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:03.291
- It is so cute.

00:01:03.291 --> 00:01:04.855
- [Voiceover] OK, while that is adorable,

00:01:04.855 --> 00:01:06.968
we need to be making
more conscious efforts,

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:09.447
like turning off the water
when we wash our hands,

00:01:09.447 --> 00:01:11.316
or taking shorter showers,

00:01:11.316 --> 00:01:12.353
like this woman.

00:01:12.353 --> 00:01:13.632
- To conserve water,

00:01:13.632 --> 00:01:16.761
I'm only taking showers
for five minutes tops.

00:01:16.761 --> 00:01:18.793
- [Voiceover] And she's starting today.

00:01:18.793 --> 00:01:21.536
- Well, actually I'm probably
gonna be starting tomorrow

00:01:21.536 --> 00:01:23.222
'cause I've got a huge date tonight,

00:01:23.222 --> 00:01:25.498
so probably gonna be at least 40 minutes,

00:01:25.498 --> 00:01:26.574
if you know what I'm saying.

00:01:26.574 --> 00:01:28.565
- [Voiceover] OK, this
last guy, he's normal.

00:01:28.565 --> 00:01:31.308
What are you doing to end
the water crisis, sir?

00:01:31.308 --> 00:01:32.425
- A drought?

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:34.640
I thought this was an
audition for The Walking Dead.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:36.490
- [Voiceover] No, I said if we didn't do

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:39.338
this PSA, we all might be dead.

00:01:39.338 --> 00:01:40.719
- I still get paid though, right?

00:01:40.719 --> 00:01:41.593
- [Voiceover] You know what, I quit.

00:01:41.593 --> 00:01:42.854
I quit.

00:01:42.854 --> 00:01:47.854
("Innovating the Future")

